    "text": "To calculate the area of a triangle, you can use the formula for the area of a triangle: \n\n\\[  \\text{Area} = \\frac{text{base} \\times \\text{height} }{2} \\]\n\nHere's the implementation of the function provided:\n\n```python\ndef triangle_area(a, h):\n    \"\"\"Given length of a side and height return area of a triangle.\n    >>> triangle_area(5, 3)\n    7.5\n    \"\"\"\n    return 0.5 * a * h\n\n# Example usage\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import doctest\n    doctest.testmod()\n```\n\nThis function calculates the area of a triangle given the length of the base `a` and the height `h`. The provided example demonstrates how to use and test the function",
